    "issue_alignment": "Upstream fix 5bffcdd304f3 ('decode: check decode_R13_2000 invalid classes') adds, right before the classes sentinel memcmp, a check that dat->byte+16 <= dat->size and section address+size <= dat->size, skipping the classes section (goto handles_section) when they fail. The PoC sets the Classes section (section[1]) address to 0xFFFFFFF0 and size to 0x20: the earlier section-record guard at line 924 wraps the 32-bit sum to 0x10 and lets it pass, after which the unvalidated address is used in the memcmp, reading 16 bytes out of bounds (heap-buffer-overflow)."
